From d0aa9084693fe23d4b3f7c472272050313a9f52a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ss3ds <ss3ds@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:17:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ss3ds: drop dangling pokeheartgold-slop symlink (breaks
 first-time builds)

Patch 0134 added port/soulsilver-research/pokeheartgold-slop as a symlink to /tmp/ps/pokeheartgold-slop, an absolute path from a dev machine that does not exist on a fresh computer. Staging copies the whole port tree into the build tree preserving symlinks, so the staged tree ends up with a dangling link exactly where the prepare step rsyncs the real decompilation in, and rsync aborts with 'File exists'. Nothing in the repo reads this link; the build fetches the decompilation itself. Dropping it fixes first-time builds.
---
 port/soulsilver-research/pokeheartgold-slop | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)
 delete mode 120000 port/soulsilver-research/pokeheartgold-slop

diff --git a/port/soulsilver-research/pokeheartgold-slop b/port/soulsilver-research/pokeheartgold-slop
deleted file mode 120000
index 4fe8ee0..0000000
--- a/port/soulsilver-research/pokeheartgold-slop
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1 +0,0 @@
-/tmp/ps/pokeheartgold-slop
\ No newline at end of file
-- 
2.43.0

